# Line endings are load-bearing here, not cosmetic.
#
# The vendored artifacts under registry/, parity/, wasm/ and firmware/ are
# verified by SHA-256 against the core agent repository. Git's autocrlf is on by
# default in the Windows installer, so without this file a fresh Windows clone
# rewrites every text artifact to CRLF, every hash changes, and the drift gate
# reports the planner implementations as disagreeing when nothing has diverged
# at all. That was true of this repository from its first commit: `git clone`
# followed by `sync_upstream.py check` failed on Windows, on the one claim the
# README leads with.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` stores text as LF and checks it out as LF everywhere, so
# the working tree, the repository and the upstream copy always agree. Matches
# the core agent's own .gitattributes, which is the point.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files must stay CRLF to run at all.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Never normalise or diff these as text.
*.wasm binary
*.db   binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
*.bin  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
